1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,266
Meet Atlas Office.

2
00:00:01,266 --> 00:00:07,316
One request brings the team together to prepare a Chengdu food and tea product launch.

3
00:00:07,316 --> 00:00:13,506
This is a business simulation using a real model connection and executable local skills.

4
00:00:13,506 --> 00:00:19,766
Atlas chooses the work, assigns colleagues, runs the tools, and creates the deliverables.

5
00:00:20,966 --> 00:00:24,797
Atlas turns the request into a visible execution plan.

6
00:00:24,797 --> 00:00:29,835
Each step has an actual skill, an assigned colleague, and dependencies.

7
00:00:29,835 --> 00:00:33,808
The model reads the skill contracts before it uses them.

8
00:00:33,808 --> 00:00:39,697
The plan and progress come from the running agent, not a prewritten video sequence.

9
00:00:40,897 --> 00:00:43,021
The first results are arriving.

10
00:00:43,021 --> 00:00:49,667
Atlas supplies the skill inputs itself and delegates to colleagues whose profiles allow the work.

11
00:00:49,667 --> 00:00:54,325
Every call is recorded with its assignee, outcome, and elapsed time.

12
00:00:54,325 --> 00:00:58,093
Completed results become context for the next decision.

13
00:00:59,293 --> 00:01:01,911
The agent continues across the company.

14
00:01:01,911 --> 00:01:09,026
Planning, responsibilities, capacity and commercial decisions are handled through the same shared runtime.

15
00:01:09,026 --> 00:01:13,590
Dependent steps can proceed only after their prerequisites complete.

16
00:01:13,590 --> 00:01:17,214
There are no manual skill forms between these actions.

17
00:01:18,414 --> 00:01:22,391
The launch takes shape as business records and real files.

18
00:01:22,391 --> 00:01:29,659
Finance calculations, project work, launch risks and management outputs are linked to recorded skill runs.

19
00:01:29,659 --> 00:01:37,680
Simulation assumptions remain visible in the content, while the document and spreadsheet generation actually execute.

20
00:01:38,880 --> 00:01:44,631
Atlas brings the completed work into the launch handoff and reusable company knowledge.

21
00:01:44,631 --> 00:01:48,795
The same request drives the workflow through its final outputs.

22
00:01:48,795 --> 00:01:55,472
The live dashboard keeps the completed work, remaining steps, generated files, and API usage visible.

23
00:01:56,672 --> 00:02:04,246
This run recorded 20 completed skill executions, covering 16 different skills and 7 colleagues.

24
00:02:04,246 --> 00:02:05,920
It produced 10 files.

25
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:10,943
The dashboard also reports 24 model requests and 26 tool calls.

26
00:02:10,943 --> 00:02:16,922
These are measured results from this run, not projected productivity gains.

27
00:02:18,122 --> 00:02:21,327
Every completed step links to its actual result.

28
00:02:21,327 --> 00:02:28,537
The activity record keeps the inputs and outputs, while the file library contains the generated launch pack.

29
00:02:28,537 --> 00:02:34,279
You can reopen the conversation later and inspect the same persisted execution record.

30
00:02:35,479 --> 00:02:44,791
Atlas Office makes agent work inspectable: one brief, a delegated plan, executable skills, and a finished set of business outputs.

31
00:02:44,791 --> 00:02:53,817
The GitHub repository includes the application, sixty-nine skill contracts, the API reference, and the evidence from this run.

32
00:02:53,817 --> 00:03:00,264
The business launch is simulated; the agent execution and generated deliverables are real.
